# Service navigation

Provide stable, named routes between the main areas of a service.

## Keep route selection separate from identity

The [header family](header.html#identity-and-navigation-have-separate-responsibilities) owns identity and home-link behaviour. This component owns the destination list, current-route marker and responsive menu. The focused [generic header](generic-header.html) does not need a navigation bar merely to share that identity contract.

## When to use

Use service navigation for a small set of destinations that remain useful across the service. It helps people understand where they are. In Home Assistant, the native sidebar already fulfils this role; do not duplicate every sidebar destination in another bar.

Use [tabs](tabs.html) for closely related views within one task and [breadcrumbs](breadcrumbs.html) for hierarchy. Keep labels short, distinct and ordered around household needs rather than internal integration names.

