## Behaviour and content

The current item has both visual emphasis and a programmatic current state. Links remain real destinations. On narrow screens the upstream component supplies a keyboard-operable menu toggle; without JavaScript the links remain available. Do not add an unrelated action to the list merely because there is space.

These standalone examples use real local section targets to make navigation inspectable without a Home Assistant connection. A production service should connect equivalent real routes and update the current marker after route changes.

## Accessibility and testing

Name the navigation landmark when a page has multiple navigation regions. Check focus after opening the mobile menu and after a route change. Test with long room names, keyboard-only use, JavaScript disabled and 200% text zoom. The current state must remain recognisable without colour.

## Source and Home Assistant boundary

[GOV.UK Service navigation](https://design-system.service.gov.uk/components/service-navigation/), reviewed 11 November 2026. The installed companion preserves native HA routing; this reference is for standalone guidance or intentionally authored custom pages.
